'''Koreasat 5A''' is a South Korean [[communications satellite]] operated by KT SAT, a subsidiary of [[KT Corporation]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://spacenews.com/40540kt-sat-picks-thales-alenia-over-orbital-sciences-for-two-satellite/|title=KT Sat Picks Thales Alenia over Orbital Sciences for Two-satellite Order|publisher=[[spacenews.com]]|date=12 May 2014|access-date=14 February 2018}}</ref> On 30 October 2017, it was launched on Falcon 9 Block 4 rocket.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.nasaspaceflight.com/2017/10/falcon-9-koreasat-5a-nasa-approves-flown-boosters/|title=SpaceX Falcon 9 successfully launches Koreasat 5A|publisher=[[Nasaspaceflight.com]]|date=30 October 2017|access-date=14 February 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.space.com/38612-spacex-koreasat-5a-satellite-launch-rocket-landing-photos.html|title=In Photos: SpaceX Launches Koreasat-5A Satellite, Lands Falcon 9 Rocket|publisher=[[Space.com]]|date=30 October 2017|access-date=14 February 2018}}</ref>

